WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.601
-Thank you for coming
back to the show.

00:00:02.601 --> 00:00:03.667
It's nice to see you in person.
-It's very exciting.

00:00:03.667 --> 00:00:05.167
Yes, you're back!
-You look good, buddy.

00:00:05.167 --> 00:00:06.734
-You've been back for a while
but I'm back with you.

00:00:06.734 --> 00:00:08.067
So now we can start.
-Now we are back.

00:00:08.067 --> 00:00:09.601
-Now the show is back.

00:00:09.601 --> 00:00:10.934
-I'm seeing you up
on the big screen.

00:00:10.934 --> 00:00:13.400
-Oh.
-I saw you in "Doctor Strange."

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:14.601
-Yes.
-You had a --

00:00:14.601 --> 00:00:15.701
[ Audience cheers ]
Right?

00:00:15.701 --> 00:00:16.767
Yeah, you know what
I'm talking about.

00:00:16.767 --> 00:00:18.400
We all saw that.

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:20.400
-But three people are like,
"spoiler alert."

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:21.934
Like, super bummed.
-Yeah.

00:00:21.934 --> 00:00:23.801
Three people plug your ears.

00:00:23.801 --> 00:00:26.133
But you're in it
for a little bit.

00:00:26.133 --> 00:00:28.067
-How dare you.
It was a big moment for me.

00:00:28.067 --> 00:00:29.367
-No, sorry.

00:00:29.367 --> 00:00:30.834
-It was a big moment for me,
but that's fine, yeah.

00:00:30.834 --> 00:00:33.534
Okay.
-But I mean -- but a little bit

00:00:33.534 --> 00:00:36.000
of the magic from the movie
was from your scenes.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:37.868
-That's right, yes.
No, I know, yes.

00:00:37.868 --> 00:00:39.267
-But everyone freaked out.

00:00:39.267 --> 00:00:41.834
You were Reed Richards
from Fantastic Four.

00:00:41.834 --> 00:00:43.300
-Yes.
-Mr. Fantastic.

00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:45.000
-I was.
-We all freaked out.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:47.467
The audience I was in, everyone
was like, "Whaaat?"

00:00:47.467 --> 00:00:49.868
-Thank you.
-"We love this!"

00:00:49.868 --> 00:00:51.300
-I actually asked.
I called and I was like,

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:52.968
"Did they go, 'Whaaaa?'"
-Yes.

00:00:52.968 --> 00:00:54.100
-And they said yes.
-We all did.

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:55.667
-Yes, they said yeah.

00:00:55.667 --> 00:00:58.701
-Comic-Con, they just announced
all these new movies and they

00:00:58.701 --> 00:01:00.701
announced that there's going to
be a Fantastic Four movie.

00:01:00.701 --> 00:01:02.667
You're not allowed to say
anything.
-Nope.

00:01:02.667 --> 00:01:04.901
-I'm not allowed to
really ask you.
-Right.

00:01:04.901 --> 00:01:06.634
-But...
[ Laughter ]

00:01:06.634 --> 00:01:07.934
You think?

00:01:07.934 --> 00:01:09.534
[ Laughter ]

00:01:09.534 --> 00:01:10.868
You think?
-Do you think?

00:01:10.868 --> 00:01:12.968
-Do you think? Could one think?

00:01:12.968 --> 00:01:15.033
Could one think?
-Seriously, what have you heard?

00:01:15.033 --> 00:01:16.667
I need to know.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:16.667 --> 00:01:17.701
-They don't tell you anything?

00:01:17.701 --> 00:01:18.868
-They don't tell you anything,
no.

00:01:18.868 --> 00:01:20.334
-Until right before you're about
to do it.

00:01:20.334 --> 00:01:21.634
-That's right.

00:01:21.634 --> 00:01:23.501
-And there's also a rumor
that your wife,

00:01:23.501 --> 00:01:25.534
Emily Blunt, will play
Sue Storm.

00:01:25.534 --> 00:01:28.701
-Oh.
[ Audience ohs ]

00:01:28.701 --> 00:01:30.801
You think?
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:30.801 --> 00:01:32.634
You think?

00:01:32.634 --> 00:01:35.400
-Jimmy, I'm going to tell you on
your show...

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:36.968
-Oh!
-It's --

00:01:36.968 --> 00:01:38.734
-Oh, my gosh.
Someone killed him right now.

00:01:38.734 --> 00:01:41.701
Could we get a medic?
That's acting right there.

00:01:41.701 --> 00:01:44.501
-No, it's actually
a Marvel dart.

00:01:44.501 --> 00:01:46.934
-There's a guy walking around.
-Yeah, exactly.

00:01:46.934 --> 00:01:48.834
-I know you're a great actor,

00:01:48.834 --> 00:01:50.267
but you're also a great writer
and director.

00:01:50.267 --> 00:01:51.801
-Thank you.
-You've been busy, busy, busy.

00:01:51.801 --> 00:01:55.267
-I got to come here more often.
This is boosting my personality.

00:01:55.267 --> 00:01:58.934
-No, but you just finished
writing and I think you're about

00:01:58.934 --> 00:02:00.868
to direct a movie called
"Imaginary Friends"?

00:02:00.868 --> 00:02:05.033
-Yes, it's called "If," and it's
with Mr. Ryan Reynolds.

00:02:05.033 --> 00:02:07.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:07.300 --> 00:02:10.801
He's an indie guy,
and this unbelievable actress

00:02:10.801 --> 00:02:12.601
named Cailey Fleming.
If anybody watches

00:02:12.601 --> 00:02:14.734
"The Walking Dead,"
she's on "Walking Dead," yeah.

00:02:14.734 --> 00:02:17.367
[ Cheers and applause ]
And it's official.

00:02:17.367 --> 00:02:19.234
Emily met her, saw her,
and was like,

00:02:19.234 --> 00:02:21.434
"She's the best actress ever."So
that's it. It's done. It's over.

00:02:21.434 --> 00:02:22.667
-That's it?
That is the best actress?

00:02:22.667 --> 00:02:25.033
-That's it. We got best actress
on the planet.

00:02:25.033 --> 00:02:26.767
-But you're reuniting with
Steve Carell.

00:02:26.767 --> 00:02:28.968
-Yeah. I should have started
with this is

00:02:28.968 --> 00:02:30.634
"The Office" reunion movie.

00:02:30.634 --> 00:02:33.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:33.567 --> 00:02:35.701
-This is "The Office"
reunion movie.

00:02:35.701 --> 00:02:37.734
-Yes.
-Wow, no, it's not that at all.

00:02:37.734 --> 00:02:39.601
-Nope, it's not, no.
-Well, what is "If"?

00:02:39.601 --> 00:02:40.934
What is "Imaginary Friends?"

00:02:40.934 --> 00:02:43.400
-"If" is basically a movie
about imaginary friends.

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:46.767
And yes, they are
these adorable, fun ideas

00:02:46.767 --> 00:02:49.701
that kids have, but really, they
are also time capsules for all

00:02:49.701 --> 00:02:52.400
of our ambitions, our dreams,
our hopes when we're kids.

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:54.868
So the movie is about what
if we could tap back into that?

00:02:54.868 --> 00:02:56.601
-Ah, I love it.
I love the way you think, bud.

00:02:56.601 --> 00:02:59.000
-Aw. Aww.

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:00.467
It's a horror movie.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:00.467 --> 00:03:02.100
-No, it is not a horror --
It's a nice --

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:03.801
-It's terrifying.

00:03:03.801 --> 00:03:05.501
-There was something that was
going around the Internet.

00:03:05.501 --> 00:03:06.667
I just wanted to ask you
about this.

00:03:06.667 --> 00:03:08.567
-The Internet is always right.
-Thank you.

00:03:08.567 --> 00:03:11.567
It says, "'The Office' --
Is Jim really the villain?"

00:03:11.567 --> 00:03:12.968
[ Laughter ]

00:03:12.968 --> 00:03:14.367
-Wait, what, did you make
that up?

00:03:14.367 --> 00:03:16.801
-No, I did not make it up.
We all decided --

00:03:16.801 --> 00:03:19.000
-It's on a card.
-Yeah, I made the card.

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:21.133
I made the card,
but we all voted.

00:03:21.133 --> 00:03:23.834
-What?
-93% agree with this.

00:03:23.834 --> 00:03:25.133
[ Laughter ]

00:03:25.133 --> 00:03:28.567
-Guys, we were doing so well.
-Did you manipulate Pam?

00:03:28.567 --> 00:03:30.334
From the beginning?

00:03:30.334 --> 00:03:33.067
-When you ask it like that,
it makes me uncomfortable.

00:03:33.067 --> 00:03:34.701
-Yeah, it's true, I've never
done that before.

00:03:34.701 --> 00:03:36.767
-"Did you manipulate Pam?"
[ Laughter ]

00:03:36.767 --> 00:03:39.601
-[ Funny voice ]
Did you manipulate Pam?

00:03:39.601 --> 00:03:41.634
[ Normal voice ]
I don't even know what voice
I was doing, I'm sorry.

00:03:41.634 --> 00:03:43.234
-Can you imagine if that's what
it was?

00:03:43.234 --> 00:03:45.567
-[ Funny voice ] What, my voice?
[ Laughter ]

00:03:45.567 --> 00:03:48.567
John Krasinski, could you talk
about Pam?

00:03:48.567 --> 00:03:50.667
[ Laughter ]
Please.

00:03:50.667 --> 00:03:53.400
-Were you at Comic-Con?
-Please talk about Pam.

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:54.434
[ Laughter ]

00:03:54.434 --> 00:03:56.734
We'd love it told.

00:03:56.734 --> 00:03:59.000
-You're getting progressively
more British.

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:02.834
[ Laughter ]
-We want to know about Pam.

00:04:02.834 --> 00:04:06.200
-The fear in your eyes
as the voice took over.

00:04:06.200 --> 00:04:08.667
-[ Normal voice ] That's
the best acting I've ever done.

00:04:08.667 --> 00:04:10.701
I don't know why --
Why would anyone do this?

00:04:10.701 --> 00:04:12.634
Jim is one of the most loveable
characters

00:04:12.634 --> 00:04:13.868
and funny characters
in the world.

00:04:13.868 --> 00:04:15.901
This is so not true.
This is garbage.

00:04:15.901 --> 00:04:18.501
-Well, they're on to me because
I played it as a supervillain.

00:04:18.501 --> 00:04:20.367
[ Laughter ]

00:04:20.367 --> 00:04:22.868
That's why I did "Fantastic
Four," to balance it out.

00:04:22.868 --> 00:04:27.334
I had already done the villain.
-Let's talk about "Super-Pets."

00:04:27.334 --> 00:04:29.801
This is a big deal.
You get to voice Superman.

00:04:29.801 --> 00:04:31.300
-Yes.
-Is this one of those things,

00:04:31.300 --> 00:04:35.734
the same as the Marvel thing,
they call up, who is it? Kevin?

00:04:35.734 --> 00:04:37.100
-Kevin Feige's from Marvel,
yeah.

00:04:37.100 --> 00:04:39.567
-He calls you up and he's like
[Deep voice] "Hey."

00:04:39.567 --> 00:04:41.868
[ Laughter ]
John, how you doing, buddy?

00:04:41.868 --> 00:04:43.267
Hey, it's me, Kevin Feige."

00:04:43.267 --> 00:04:44.968
-Can you take a TV time-out?
We got to talk about this.

00:04:44.968 --> 00:04:47.267
-"It's Kevin Feige.
It's Kevin Feige."

00:04:47.267 --> 00:04:49.133
-Oh, no, now it's Will Arnett.

00:04:49.133 --> 00:04:51.234
[ Laughter ]

00:04:51.234 --> 00:04:54.267
-Hey, it's Will.
-Hey, man.

00:04:54.267 --> 00:04:56.667
-Hey, man. Hey, man. Hey, man.
You want to do it?

00:04:56.667 --> 00:04:59.400
-Hey, man, do you want to be
Mr. Fantastic?

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:00.467
[ Laughter ]

00:05:00.467 --> 00:05:02.267
-Hey, man.
-Yeah.

00:05:02.267 --> 00:05:04.968
-You don't? Oh, you don't?

00:05:04.968 --> 00:05:06.334
Oh, you don't want to be
Mr. Fantastic?

00:05:06.334 --> 00:05:08.501
Oh, you don't? Oh, really?

00:05:08.501 --> 00:05:10.934
-Sean will do it.
-Oh, you want to be Superman?

00:05:10.934 --> 00:05:15.167
Yeah, you should go to DC.
Go do DC.

00:05:15.167 --> 00:05:17.234
-Do DC.

00:05:17.234 --> 00:05:20.767
[ Laughter ]
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:20.767 --> 00:05:22.667
-None of that is useable.

00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:26.601
-[ Normal voice ]
We have to air it.

00:05:26.601 --> 00:05:29.200
We have to air it.
-If only for Will.

00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:31.534
-We have to air it
just for Will.

00:05:31.534 --> 00:05:32.968
But then you get to do this.

00:05:32.968 --> 00:05:35.234
Dude, you get to play Superman.
It's unbelievable.

00:05:35.234 --> 00:05:37.467
And this is like a great movie
the whole family will love.

00:05:37.467 --> 00:05:39.701
It's you, Kevin Hart,
Dwayne Johnson.

00:05:39.701 --> 00:05:41.934
-Yes.
-The cast is insane.

00:05:41.934 --> 00:05:44.767
It's super funny.
But you get to play Superman,

00:05:44.767 --> 00:05:47.534
and then kind of your pets
have to save the world.

00:05:47.534 --> 00:05:50.334
-Yes, which, at first, I was
really excited to play Superman

00:05:50.334 --> 00:05:52.567
until they made my dog

00:05:52.567 --> 00:05:55.601
bigger than me
and somehow more handsome?

00:05:55.601 --> 00:05:57.801
It's played by Dwayne "The Rock"
Johnson, by the way,

00:05:57.801 --> 00:06:00.167
who called and was like,
"Hey, will you do 'Super-Pets'?

00:06:00.167 --> 00:06:03.667
Make the dog cooler. Oh, it's
a yes? Okay, great. Perfect."

00:06:03.667 --> 00:06:05.300
-And have you taken
your daughters to see this?

00:06:05.300 --> 00:06:07.367
-They loved it. It was --

00:06:07.367 --> 00:06:09.100
They were laughing
very, very hard.

00:06:09.100 --> 00:06:11.601
I think up until now
they didn't believe

00:06:11.601 --> 00:06:13.200
I actually was in the business.

00:06:13.200 --> 00:06:14.834
'Cause they've never seen
anything I've done.

00:06:14.834 --> 00:06:17.100
So it's like, "Quiet Place,"
not yet.

00:06:17.100 --> 00:06:19.100
"Jack Ryan," things like that,
nope.

00:06:19.100 --> 00:06:20.734
-And this is the perfect movie
to take them to see.

00:06:20.734 --> 00:06:22.868
-They were like, "Wow, you're
not an accountant."

00:06:22.868 --> 00:06:24.801
[ Laughter ]

00:06:24.801 --> 00:06:28.567
-I want to show everyone a clip.
Here's John Krasinski

00:06:28.567 --> 00:06:31.534
as Superman in "DC League of
Super-Pets."

00:06:31.534 --> 00:06:32.801
Take a look at this.

00:06:32.801 --> 00:06:34.767
-From Metropolis, I'm Lois Lane.

00:06:34.767 --> 00:06:36.267
-Hey, Lois!

00:06:38.400 --> 00:06:43.334
I know you like these, so I got
you one from actual Paris.

00:06:43.334 --> 00:06:45.067
I don't know why I said it
like that.

00:06:45.067 --> 00:06:48.400
-And I got you one of these
from 43rd Street,

00:06:48.400 --> 00:06:50.901
which is like a full
three blocks out of my way.

00:06:50.901 --> 00:06:52.234
-During rush hour?

00:06:52.234 --> 00:06:54.133
Wow, that's like me
flying to Mars.

00:06:54.133 --> 00:06:56.100
-What, you can fly?

00:06:56.100 --> 00:06:58.367
I always thought the cape was
just a cute accessory.

00:06:58.367 --> 00:07:00.834
-Oh, so you think I'm cute?

00:07:00.834 --> 00:07:03.467
-I said the cape was cute.

00:07:03.467 --> 00:07:05.601
-[ Sighs ]
You think I'm cute.

00:07:07.133 --> 00:07:08.701
-Are we licking faces right now?

00:07:08.701 --> 00:07:10.901
Because if we're licking faces,
I got to get in on --

00:07:10.901 --> 00:07:12.834
[ Barking ]

00:07:12.834 --> 00:07:14.467
-Yeah, come on.
-Yeah!

00:07:14.467 --> 00:07:16.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:16.033 --> 00:07:17.501
-John Krasinski, everybody!

00:07:17.501 --> 00:07:20.567
"DC League of Super-Pets" hits
theaters Friday.

00:07:20.567 --> 00:07:23.634
We'll be right back with
Rege-Jean Page. Stick around.

